athens "element modified after free" hunt: the writer is still unknown.
DPM exclusion (0168 window) did not stop it. This patch adds:

* bsd/dev/sweet_watch.c - wired canary pages re-verified every ~100 ms after a
  physical cache flush; on mismatch prints VA+PA+dump (the PA distribution is
  the fingerprint: clustered = a bus-master window, uniform = wild CPU
  pointer) and arms an ARM64 store watchpoint on the corrupted granule (a
  cyclic CPU writer panics with a backtrace; a bus master never trips it).
  Boot args: sweetwatch=0|1|2 (default 1), sweetwatch_n=N (default 128).
* osfmk/kern/zalloc.c - zalloc_uaf_panic reports the element physical
  address (pmap_find_phys) into the console + SWEETPAN tag, and honours
  sweetuaf=1: re-zero and continue to collect more hits per boot.

